  <body>
    <a href="/">&larr; Back to catalog</a>
    <h1>Submit a component</h1>
    <p>
      This is not a form — DecDev is a git-based catalog. Every component is a plain YAML file
      reviewed through a normal pull request.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>Fork the repository.</li>
      <li>
        Add a file at <code>components/&lt;your-slug&gt;.yaml</code> following the schema in
        <code>specs/01-capability-spec-format.md</code> — every field, its type, and the required
        <code>license</code>/<code>provenance</code> rules are documented there.
      </li>
      <li>
        Build the CLI once (<code>cargo install --path cli</code>), then run
        <code>decdev validate</code> locally — it runs the exact same check CI will run on your
        PR.
      </li>
      <li>Open a pull request.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Every <code>implementations[].url</code> you list must be a real link you've personally
      verified resolves — see <code>specs/01-capability-spec-format.md</code> for why this is a
      hard requirement, not a suggestion.
    </p>
    <p>
      Full details, including the human-review gate for anything derived from proprietary source
      analysis, are in <code>CONTRIBUTING.md</code>.
    </p>
  </body>
